codex
Section 5 supplies a better native family than the initial “arbitrary tree models” idea: height-one posets whose order is the intersection of three interval orders. I can sample the three interval orders first, derive the poset, and use the three orders as an exact witness; the paper’s reduction uses precisely those three orders along the three parallel edges of \(\Delta^+\). I’m prototyping this route against a cycle-pruning backtracker—the natural exact recognition attack—before committing to it.
